# Offline

The POC must keep working with the network disabled after the service worker has installed.

- Register a service worker from the site root (`sw.js`) so its scope covers the whole app.
- Precache every file the app needs: HTML, CSS, JS, images, fonts, data files, and everything in `vendor/`.
- On install, cache that full list. Serve cached responses while offline. App code and libraries must not depend on a network fetch.
- When you add, rename, or remove a file or dependency, update the precache list in the same change and bump the cache name.
- Do not call remote APIs for core behavior. If a feature needs data, ship that data in the repo and cache it.
- Verify offline programmatically: load the site once so the worker installs, disable the network, reload, and assert that the page still responds and the console has no errors.
